## Authoring rules for the remaining ten

1. **Look up the row first.** If the row says NONE, the lesson must *say so* — the declared-gap paragraph is part of the content, exactly as in Unit 5's scholarly-honesty note.
2. **Never let a vendor doc pose as research.** Astro/R3F/Workbox documentation grounds *how*, never *why this sequence teaches well*.
3. **Follow the Unit 5/6 standard**: labelled code blocks, TTOD quote by ID, `relative_url` links, dated version pins, `{% raw %}` on any fence containing `{{`.
4. **Cite by coat·node·page.** No citation without a node — see [`.cursor/rules/lesson-publishing-integrity.mdc`](../../.cursor/rules/lesson-publishing-integrity.mdc).
5. **The gaps are the FE II thesis.** Six of twelve units have no pedagogical evidence. That is not a weakness to hide — it is what makes FE II a declared pilot and a research site ([`../fe-research-line.mdc`](../fe-research-line.mdc)).

